<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-chrysomallon-squamiferum-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 2.0 nm on Chrysomallon squamiferum (Pass 1) — MorphoEval overall 72.7/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 integrates one Schnakenberg field (a=0.062, b=1.084, D_v/D_u=36, seed 3147) with diffusivities chosen so the onset wavenumber is 2π/2.0 nm. Closed-form σ(k) matches numpy eigenvalues at r=1.0. The PDE radial peak is 2.52 nm, not 2.0 nm. The paratype photograph is the anatomical canvas. No parameter sweep, no equal-diffusion ablation, and no KS comparison against the specimen were run. Overall 72.7/100 (faithfulness 67.3, reproducibility 85.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 6f01b4c5e4c9fa53e8bf2c8825be8b7ccb7fba3c; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 74, Morphological realism / specimen match 76, Parameter expressivity 46, Morphometric validation 58, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 82, Reproducibility package 84. Output judged: docs/media/chrysomallon_squamiferum_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-chrysomallon-squamiferum-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 6f01b4c5e4c9fa53e8bf2c8825be8b7ccb7fba3c, image/png, 505249 B, 1248×960 px, artifact_sha256 f78b2d8abd16f668188f1f75d9a33d749cbc8e44b01e0b5814be146d1e378f5d (sha256 f78b2d8abd16f668188f1f75d9a33d749cbc8e44b01e0b5814be146d1e378f5d), spec_fingerprint e0865ee451716d4a3fa5bd6b6983a8391e5da7f8dc195fece7fe187c823b6b31. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 5a948670023100da2057a11d9e5a60a14e996d44987bb98d540f2f6d1fbf8647; artifact_sha256: f78b2d8abd16f668188f1f75d9a33d749cbc8e44b01e0b5814be146d1e378f5d; input_dataset_sha256: {chrysomallon_squamiferum_specimen.jpg=0312a80d873d68d2..., paper_citations.bib=63b7c502b791e3c1..., scout_manifest.json=ea589eba9289f0c9...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Iron-sulfide sclerites (Warén 2003) and multilayer armor mechanics (Yao 2010) | Turing wavenumber selection (Turing 1952) and Schnakenberg kinetics (1979) | Greigite cubic cell near 0.988 nm (Skinner, Erd and Grimaldi 1964); reconstructed_in_script: Onset k_c solved for D_u at λ=2.0 nm and one IMEX Schnakenberg integration | Activator painted on the MNHN-IM-2000-30072 sclerite mask; transfer_boundary: No source measures a 2.0 nm pigment stripe on this snail. 2.0 nm is the assigned detail-scale wavelength, about two greigite cells.; does_not_claim: Does not claim Yao et al. 2010 stated a reaction-diffusion equation | Does not claim the Pass 1 PDE peak equals 2.0 nm | Does not claim a successor chronospecies after the Holocene animal." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Sweep target wavelength (diffusivity scale) and report Pearson r and RMSE of PDE radial-FFT peaks against the targets.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Run an equal-diffusion ablation (D_u=D_v) and report the amplitude ratio against the patterned field.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Segment the paratype and compare it to the render with structure-tensor coherency, circularity, and a KS test.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Retune diffusivities so the maximum of σ(k), not the onset formula, sits on 2.0 nm, and require the PDE peak within 8%.'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 7.27e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

